From: superslor <289523157+superslor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:21:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] speculative: a separate draft model gets its own
 micro-batch (LLAMA_SPEC_DRAFT_UBATCH)

Its compute buffer scales with n_ubatch (Gemma 4 12B's drafter: 1305 MiB at 2048, 326 at 512), which
kept it from fitting beside the target on a 16 GB card; the target keeps its -ub. Default 512, 0 = the
target's. MI25, Gemma 4 12B with its QAT drafter, 2 drafts: short 36.5 -> 47.8 t/s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TS8XWm5bp2cWmYvbQ5tTBK
---
 common/speculative.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/common/speculative.cpp b/common/speculative.cpp
index f62c2ef29..a191ae647 100644
--- a/common/speculative.cpp
+++ b/common/speculative.cpp
@@ -3209,6 +3209,18 @@ common_speculative_init_result::common_speculative_init_result(
 
         pimpl->model.reset(model_dft);
 
+        // a separate draft model gets its own, smaller micro-batch. Its compute buffer scales with n_ubatch
+        // (Gemma 4 12B's drafter: 1305 MiB at 2048, 326 at 512), and only that much stopped it fitting beside the
+        // target on a 16 GB card; the target keeps its own n_ubatch, so prompt reading is unchanged.
+        // LLAMA_SPEC_DRAFT_UBATCH=N sets it (0 = the target's).
+        {
+            const char * e  = std::getenv("LLAMA_SPEC_DRAFT_UBATCH");
+            const int    ub = e ? std::atoi(e) : 512;
+            if (ub > 0 && (uint32_t) ub < cparams.n_ubatch) {
+                cparams.n_ubatch = ub;
+            }
+        }
+
         const char * greedy_env = std::getenv("LLAMA_DSPARK_GREEDY_IDS");
         if (greedy_env && std::strcmp(greedy_env, "1") == 0) {
             llama_dspark_meta meta;
